WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:03.330
YouTube might be best known for short viral
clips.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:07.479
But you may not know that YouTube also offers
thousands of free movies as well.

00:00:07.479 --> 00:00:11.660
Yes, on YouTube you can watch everything from
indie films uploaded by their creators, to

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:15.960
modern movies released for free by major studios,
to classic films that are now in the public

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:16.960
domain.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.850
In fact, there are so many options it can
be hard to know where to start.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:24.320
That's why we've put together this list of
some of the best free movies on YouTube.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.619
Kung Fury

00:00:25.619 --> 00:00:30.199
This comedy-action indie was produced as a
tribute to the awesome action films of the

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:31.230
1980s.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:36.180
In the film, a Miami detective is simultaneously
struck by lightning and bitten by a cobra

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:41.200
— which, obviously, gives him superhuman
Kung Fu powers.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:44.400
"Game over."

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:53.080
He uses the new power granted to him to clean
up the streets of Miami.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:58.720
But our hero faces his worst adversary yet
when he comes face-to-face with Kung Fu master...Adolf

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.660
Hitler.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.280
Ka-pow!

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:08.100
Margot at the Wedding

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.440
This dark comedy follows the story of Margot
and her son Claude as they visit Margot's

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:17.550
sister Pauline for her wedding to the unsuccessful
artist and musician Malcolm.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:22.440
"Expectation just turns to disappointment
so ultimately I'd rather not share."

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.950
But the plot is secondary to the awesome cast:
it features Nicole Kidman as Margot, Jennifer

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:31.780
Jason-Leigh as Pauline, and a hilarious performance
from Jack Black in the role of the unmotivated

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.360
and socially inept Malcolm.

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:38.200
It's a winner.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.240
Four Horsemen

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:47.840
In this independent British documentary, the
filmmakers take a hard look at current banking

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.260
and economic practices in Western countries,
as well as the War on Terror, and how it all

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.210
connects to our monetary policies.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.550
Time Out London critic Derek Adams wrote:

00:01:56.550 --> 00:02:00.960
"Instead of bombarding us with sensational
imagery and scaremongering, this competently

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.840
narrated, intelligibly structured and cleverly
illustrated film presents its case via a succession

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:09.119
of insights from a group of smart, rational
orators."

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:12.920
In other words, it's not exactly your typical
YouTube video…

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:18.360
"Leave me alone, please."

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.360
Slacker

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:25.400
Not to be confused with the 2002 movie Slackers,
this 1991 independent comedy-drama marked

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:30.100
the directorial debut of Richard Linklater,
who would go on to direct classics like Boyhood

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.349
and Dazed and Confused.

00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:35.880
"That's what I like about these high school
girls, man.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.840
I get older they stay the same age."

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.200
Featuring a uniquely unstructured storyline,
Slacker is a slice of time—a day in the

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.430
life of multiple 20-something misfits as they
drift through Austin, Texas.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:55.010
Shot with a single 16mm camera on a micro
budget of just $23,000, many filmmakers — including

00:02:55.010 --> 00:02:59.780
Kevin Smith — have cited Slacker as a major
source of inspiration and the start of the

00:02:59.780 --> 00:03:02.150
'90s independent movie movement.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:05.380
"The people they need, like scientist, you
heard about that.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:08.670
All the missing scientist around the world
and those that mysteriously dying.

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:10.750
That's all part of the recruiting process.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.530
I really hope you friend is not, well.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:17.270
They need a lot of lackeys to do the labor
though.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:18.780
So they will be looking for ordinary guys.

00:03:18.780 --> 00:03:21.989
You know, like you and me."

00:03:21.989 --> 00:03:23.430
Funny About Love

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:28.200
While Funny About Love was pretty much universally
panned by critics upon its release, it might

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:29.400
deserve another look.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:30.400
Why?

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.590
Well, it was directed by the legendary Leonard
Nimoy, stars the late, great Gene Wilder,

00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:39.050
and has an interesting take on the whole "ticking
biological clock" trope — but from a man's

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:40.100
perspective.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:44.150
Wilder's comedic genius shines through in
several places, making Funny About Love a

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:47.660
good pick for a cheap date night flick.

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:56.860
"Take this, take this thing"

00:03:57.709 --> 00:03:59.200
Night of the Living Dead

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.620
Considered by many to be the seminal zombie
movie, Night of the Living Dead has been massively

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.920
influential on the horror genre in the decades
since its release.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:12.120
George A. Romero's directorial debut is more
atmospheric than most modern zombie films,

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:16.750
focusing instead on the effects of a zombie
outbreak in a small town, with most of the

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.759
film is set within the house where the cast
members take refuge.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:24.399
"I ought to drag you out there and feed you
those things."

00:04:28.039 --> 00:04:29.699
Walking Dead's got nothing on this…

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.620
"Liar"

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:34.620
Nosferatu

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:41.400
F.W. Murnau's 1922 silent classic Nosferatu
is required watching material for all horror

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.400
fans.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:46.180
The earliest surviving example of a major
vampire film, actor Max Schreck delivers a

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:51.740
mesmerizing performance as the ghastly vampire
in this unauthorized adaptation of Bram Stoker's

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:52.740
Dracula.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:57.050
It's amazing the movie even exists, as a court
once ordered all copies to be destroyed after

00:04:57.050 --> 00:04:59.969
Stoker's estate sued for copyright infringement.

00:04:59.969 --> 00:05:04.029
But loyal fans secretly saved it and passed
copies around — making it one of the first

00:05:04.029 --> 00:05:05.750
true viral videos ever.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.830
Only fitting for the original bed intruder…

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:13.190
"So y'all need to hide yo kids, hide yo wife
and hide yo husband because they rapping everybody

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.190
out here."

00:05:14.190 --> 00:05:15.190
Thanks for watching!

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.800
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:21.309
And leave us a comment to let us know which
free YouTube film you'd recommend…

